{
  "about": [
    "The Habit fold, written as data: which passed iterations fold into a run, and the scope levels",
    "a run opens into.",
    "",
    "Both evaluators replay it. `src-tauri/tests/operations/habit_fold_conformance.rs` runs every case",
    "through `flows::rules::fold`; `src/utils/habit-fold-conformance.test.ts` runs the same cases",
    "through `foldHabitRuns`. Neither side generates this file.",
    "",
    "A case's `children` are one node's children, in order: an iteration names its Habit (`flow`), the",
    "scope `kind` its window is one unit of (null for a sub-day window), its first day (`anchor`), its",
    "window's end, whether it has `passed`, whether it was `done`, and whether it is `owed`; anything",
    "else is just an `id`. `folded` is what is drawn in their place: a node's id, or a group with its",
    "id, its `level` (`run`, or the scope level), its tally and its children. Labels and spans are",
    "drawing, and are not here."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a run folds at the threshold and reads its tally",
      "spec": "habits.md \u2014 Every run of consecutive passed iterations past the threshold folds into one node.",
      "threshold": 3,
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "i1",
          "flow": 1,
          "kind": "day",
          "anchor": "2026-09-14",
          "windowEnd": "2026-09-15T02:00:00",
          "passed": true,
          "done": true
        },
        {
          "id": "i2",
          "flow": 1,
          "kind": "day",
